 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Content Approval Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a content approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"A content approval workflow is the set of review steps a draft passes through before it is published. It names who reviews each type of content and in what order. It also says what happens after an approval or a request for changes, and it keeps a record of every decision.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build a content approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"List the content you publish and who signs off on each type. Then note which details call for an extra reviewer, such as a cited statistic or a price. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a> builds the app from that description, connected to your calendar, Slack, and CMS. Run a week of real drafts through it before the whole team switches.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the stages of a marketing approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"Most start with an editor checking the copy. A marketing approval workflow then adds a brand owner for voice and visuals, while legal or a subject expert joins only when a piece calls for one. Requests for changes go back to the author with comments attached. Approved pieces move onto the publishing calendar.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many reviewers does a marketing content approval workflow need?\", \"a\": \"Two fixed reviewers cover most routine pieces: an editor and the brand owner. Add specialists on a trigger, such as a product claim or a customer quote, instead of on every piece. Keep the marketing content approval workflow short, because each fixed stage is a queue that every draft waits in. Apps built on Emergent include every approver at no per-seat cost.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you set up a social media approval workflow with clients?\", \"a\": \"Agencies batch a week of posts into one review link instead of sending them one at a time. The client approves each post or leaves a comment, and comments return to the writer. In a good social media approval workflow, posts with no answer trigger a reminder to the account manager. A shared view shows which posts are cleared to schedule and which still wait.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a campaign approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"It approves the campaign as a whole before any single asset is reviewed. The brief, budget, and launch dates are signed off first. Each asset in a campaign approval workflow is then checked against that brief, which heads off design rounds over questions the brief should have settled. The brief itself can come from <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/document-automation'>document automation</a>, filled from the campaign request.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you keep a creative approval workflow from dragging on?\", \"a\": \"Agree on a limit for revision rounds in the brief, such as two, and count every round on each asset. When someone asks for one more, route it to a senior reviewer who decides whether it is worth the time. A creative approval workflow also moves faster when reviewers send their comments in one pass.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should marketing approval workflow software include?\", \"a\": \"It needs routing that sends each piece to the right reviewers and lets them answer from the message itself. Add reminders for stalled reviews and a searchable record of every approved version. Check how marketing approval workflow software is priced, since per-seat plans charge for every occasional reviewer. On Emergent, the approval history sits in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the steps in a design approval workflow?\", \"a\": \"A typical design approval workflow starts with a signed-off brief and first concepts. One or two revision rounds follow, and final files are checked against the brand guide before release. Store each version with its comments. A reviewer can then see what changed between rounds without digging through email.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should content approval workflows differ by content type?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A reply to a customer on social cannot wait two days for legal, while a pricing page should. Give each type its own path, short for social posts and longer for anything with claims or prices. Content approval workflows run on the same logic as any other approval workflow; only the triggers and the reviewers change.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
